// AlmaNewUserDisk.customers -- create a new user disk at SPG 
//   (Shipping version)
// edited April 22, 1982  11:56 AM, Rick Martin

// FIRST, start bfstest.boot from the NetExec.
// Do the following when in bfstest.boot
//	*partition 1
//	*Certify. How many passes? 100
//	Use both of the disks?  [y]
//	Use all 406 cylinders of the disk?  [y]
//	Use all 14 sectors of the disk?  [y]
//	*Erase.
//	*Exercise. How many passes? 10
//	Use both of the disks?  [y]
//	Use all 406 cylinders of the disk?  [y]
//	Use all 14 sectors of the disk?  [y]
//	*Partition 2
//	*Certify. How many passes? 100
//	Use both of the disks?  [y]
//	Use all 406 cylinders of the disk?  [y]
//	Use all 14 sectors of the disk?  [y]
//	*Erase.
//	*Exercise. How many passes? 10
//	Use both of the disks?  [y]
//	Use all 406 cylinders of the disk?  [y]
//	Use all 14 sectors of the disk?  [y]
//	*Quit
// (Be aware that certify seems to take about six hours. Erase
//  takes only a couple of minutes. Exercise takes about four 
//  hours.) This process will result in a much more reliable 
//  disk.

// SECOND install new operating system by typing
//	Partition number 1
//	NewOS.boot
// You should perform the following dialog - user responses
//   are enclosed in square brackets: [].
//	Do you want to install this operating system?   [y]
//	Do you want the long installation dialog?  [y]
//	Do you want to ERASE the disk before installing?  [y]
//	Type the name of a host . . get Alto programs: [Alma <return>]
//	Type the name of directory . . . 
//	. . . If the host . . . random Alto type <return>: [alto <return>]
//	Use both of the disks?  [y]
//	Use all 406 cylinders of the disk?  [y]
//	Use all 14 sectors of the disk?  [y]
//	When the disk is ready . . . : [ok]
//	Do you want to disable error . . . through the net?  [y]
//	Do you want to change memory error parameters?  [n]
//	What is your name? [Lisp]
//	Please give your disk a name:  [Partition 1]
//	Do you wish to . . . password?  [n]

// Return to the NetExec, type Partition number 2, and 
//  run NewOS again, giving the same answers, except 
//  naming the disk Partition 2.

// Return to the NetExec and run
//	MesaNetExec.boot
//	>SetVersions
//	  Germ: D0.eg
//	  Microcode: PilotCSLF.eb
//	>OthelloD0.pb
//		(Screen will go wide and will give Othello prompt: >)
//	>login
//	User: [your name]
//	Password: [your password]
//	>open connection to Alma
//	> initial microcode fetch
//	Drive Name: [rd0]
//	File Name: [<Lisp>d0>InitialAlto.eb]
//	Are you sure?  [y]
//	>Quit 
//	Are you sure?  [y]

// Now run FTP and retrieve this file onto both partitions 
//   and execute it on each partition.

delete dmt.boot dumper.boot // garbage on disk
//install swat
ftp/-E Alma login/c guest guest ^
directory/c Alto retrieve/>A InstallSwat.run Sys.Errors 
InstallSwat
Delete dumper.boot installswat.run

//Now create Lisp.virtualmem
ftp/-E Alma directory/c Alto retrieve/>A CreateFile.run 
CREATEFILE.run LISP.VIRTUALMEM 8000D

// bring over Lisp files
FTP/-E Alma ^
directory/c Lisp>Current ^
retrieve/>A LISP.run LISP.syms LISP.sysout Init.ParcPlace DolphinLispMC.Run ^
retrieve/s INIT.NoNet INIT.LISP ^
retrieve/s LispUser.customers user.cm ^
directory/c Fonts retrieve/>A ^
GACHA8.STRIKE  GACHA10.STRIKE  GACHA12.STRIKE ^
Helvetica5.strike  HELVETICA7.STRIKE  HELVETICA8.STRIKE ^
HELVETICA9.STRIKE HELVETICA10.STRIKE HELVETICA10B.STRIKE ^
HELVETICA12B.STRIKE ^
directory/c fonts retrieve/>A fonts.widths ^
directory/c Lispusers ^
retrieve/c BQUOTE.DCOM  BROWSER.DCOM  CIRCLPRINT.DCOM ^
DATABASEFNS.DCOM DECL.DCOM DEDIT.DCOM ^
DSPRINTDEF.DCOM NEWPRINTDEF.DCOM ^
GRAPHER.DCOM HANOI.DCOM  INSPECT.DCOM  LABEL.DCOM ^
LAMBDATRAN.DCOM ^
NOBOX.DCOM  PERMSTATUS.DCOM POLYGONS.DCOM ^
PRESSBITMAP.DCOM  PRINTL.DCOM SAMEDIR.DCOM SIMPLIFY.DCOM ^
SINGLEFILEINDEX.DCOM  TTYIN.DCOM ^
directory/c alto retrieve/c Scavenger.run ^

// Scavange the disk
Scavenger.run

// Have you read this command file before executing it?
// There are extensive instructions at the beginning.
// Make sure both partitions are done.
